5.1. Criterion for Opening the Conditional Chapter

The conditional thermodynamic conjecture is opened only if:

1. H_{1a} satisfied on \geq 2 families.
2. H_{1b} satisfied on \geq 2 families.
3. \max_j \mathrm{CV}_j(\lambda^\star) \leq 0.20 observed, with dual-ascent convergence below threshold on all reported points.

5.2. Possible Outcomes

Positive: Non-trivial signal on F_1 and F_3, less on F_2. Cross-family stability of \lambda^\star. Separation between MCD and B4_{\text{Pred}} under RQ1 (Value of Causal Information).

Negative: MCD \approx B4_{\text{Pred}} under matched information (confirming the algebraic equivalence). Instability of \lambda^\star. No Pareto expansion.

Mixed: Pareto expansion without q-dominance (local gain rather than distributional gain). Incomparable distributions under q-dominance.

