Remark I.3 (Heterogeneous instrumentation semantics). NVML, RAPL, and IPMI are different interfaces with different meanings, latency, aggregation, and calibration characteristics. Their telemetry streams are not assumed to be equivalent measurements of a single physical quantity. The boundary energy E_{\text{boundary}} is the primary quantity; component telemetry is an attribution layer, not a physical decomposition.

